                <pb facs="1043" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.00/699: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-06T11:00:00+02:00">June 6, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 6—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Oriental Institute and Princeton directors remaining at Antioch with Farrell; are
                    sending today to Tartous Mr. and Mrs. Braidwood and to Beirut temporarily, Mr.
                    Smith, Mr. and Mrs. Waage and Mrs. McEwen <pb facs="1044" n="1036"
                        xml:id="pg1036"/> and children. They emphasize this is only precautionary
                    and not indicative of immediate danger or probability of serious disturbances
                    and they wish to avoid if possible publication of news of departure of
                    expedition personnel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Palmer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
